      "text": "Suchitoto: Crafts and Indigo"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9564ff81b588026c738a3059d3a8e42f8cf13da04b795a0da18bade4051ea6c3",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-mwa5muwazo597oeipo",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, take a walking tour of Suchitoto, with its cobbled streets, colonial houses and Santa Lucía Church.\n\nMeet local artisan Laura Peña, who has been rolling cigars by hand for several decades. She’ll introduce you to the traditional technique and show you what goes into the craft.\n\nThen visit Pájaro Flor, a women’s artisan cooperative that preserves the tradition of dyeing fabrics with indigo. Learn about the history of the craft and make your own indigo-dyed scarf.\n\nOvernight at Hotel El Tejado. Meals: breakfast."
    },
